# SpoonBuddy - THE PUBLIC REPOSITORY. THIS TREE IS PUBLIC THE MOMENT IT IS PUSHED.
#
# Written 2026-09-03, on the developer's instruction: "can you exclude review notes and shots
# from being committed or pushed?" and "and my personal settings and files".
#
# THERE WAS NO IGNORE FILE HERE AT ALL UNTIL TODAY, and this is the tree where it
# matters most. private\app\ reaches people one step later, through a release;
# private\ is private; this is served by GitHub Pages the moment it is pushed.
# CLAUDE.md already says to treat the website as the strictest of the trees rather
# than the loosest because it is small - and it had the least protection of any.
#
# What is meant to be here is six files: the site, the licence, the readme and
# status.json. Anything else is a question, which is why private\tools\audit-areas.ps1
# is an ALLOW-LIST and this is only the second line.

# ---------------------------------------------------------- personal data --
# None of these should ever be in this tree - the app writes them to the user's
# own profile. They are named anyway, because a rule that never fires costs
# nothing and the one time it does it is somebody's health record.
spoonbuddy-log.csv
spoonbuddy-sleep.csv
spoonbuddy-settings.txt
spoonbuddy-pos.txt
spoonbuddy-current.txt
spoonbuddy-peer.txt
spoonbuddy-feedback.txt
spoonbuddy-error.log
activities.csv
stints.tsv
paced.tsv
sync-state.tsv
last-activity.txt
chart-days.txt

# NO TRAILING SLASH on backup-*, and that is the point: `backup-*/` matches
# DIRECTORIES ONLY, so a backup written as a single FILE slips past. A backup is a
# backup either way.
backup-*
backups/
logs/
local/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ renders --
# A RENDER OF THE RUNNING APP IS THE SAME DATA AS activities.csv, IN A FORM NO
# IGNORE RULE AND NO GREP CAN READ. The case this rule comes from: eight
# pictures of the running app against real records, tracked for two days, past an
# ignore file that was working perfectly and had never been told about the folder.
review-shots/
review-work/
review-notes/
screenshots/
design/screenshots/
*.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------- credentials --
google-services.json
*.keystore
*.jks
keystore.properties
.env
secrets.json
firebase-key.json

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ os --
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# AND A RULE IS A DEFAULT, NOT A REFUSAL. tools\githooks\pre-commit refuses, and
# it matches the file NAMES the app writes rather than the folders they land in.
# Install it once per clone:
#     git config core.hooksPath tools/githooks
